# Car Fuel Management Application

**An app that helps South Africans buy fuel at discounted rates based on their loyalty**

I built this app to solve a simple problem - fuel is expensive, and loyal customers should get better deals. The app tracks how often someone buys fuel through us and gives them bigger discounts the more they use the service.

## What does this app actually do?

Think of it like a fuel subscription service. You sign up, register your car, and buy fuel through us once per month. Your first purchase costs 125% of the fuel price (ouch, I know). But if you pay on time and keep using the service, your price drops - eventually down to just 25% of the fuel price.

**The discount system works like this:**

| Purchase # | What you pay |
|------------|--------------|
| 1st time | 125% of fuel price |
| 2nd purchase | 118.75% (6.25% off) |
| 3rd purchase | 112.5% (another 6.25% off) |
| ... continues ... | |
| After 12 purchases | 25% of fuel price |

Yes, you read that right. Loyal customers eventually pay only a quarter of what fuel actually costs.

## How registration works

**Step 1: Personal details**
- Name, surname, ID number, home address, car registration
- Your ID gets validated with Home Affairs (we check you're a real South African)
- Your car registration gets checked with Traffic Department (is the car roadworthy?)
- Also checked with SAPS (is the car stolen?)

**Step 2: Car details**
- Pick your car model from a dropdown list
- The system knows your fuel tank size (data from AA South Africa)
- It calculates your full tank price using current fuel prices (from PetroleumSA)

**Step 3: Accept or decline**
- You see the quotation and decide if you want to proceed
- If yes, you choose a repayment date (within 30 days)
- Payment happens via debit order or card

## The rules (important bit)

**For consistent customers (using service every month):**
- First purchase: 125% of fuel price
- Each successful on-time payment gives you 6.25% discount for next purchase
- After 12 months of consistent use, you pay only 25% of fuel price
- After one year, benefits reset but you start at 5% discount (not zero)

**For non-consistent customers (skip months):**
- Use service 4-11 times per year → 2.5% discount in year 2
- Use service less than 3 times per year → 1% discount in year 2
- You can upgrade to higher discounts if you become consistent

**One important rule:** You can only buy fuel once per month. No exceptions.

## How I built this

**Frontend:** Android (Java, XML layouts)
**Backend:** Java with file I/O for validations

The app has 4 main screens:

1. **Registration & Login** - Username and password
2. **Personal Details** - Name, ID, address, car registration
3. **Car Details** - Select model, see fuel capacity and price
4. **Payment Summary** - Quotation and repayment options

## Validations (the tricky part)

This was the hardest part to implement:

**ID Number Validation:**
- Must be a valid South African ID
- Verified through a custom "Home Affairs" validation system
- Uses Java file I/O to read from validation files

**Car Registration Validation:**
- Must match format of one of 9 South African provinces
- Verified with custom "Traffic Department" system
- Checked against "SAPS" stolen vehicle database
- All using Java file I/O strategy

**Province registration formats:**
- Gauteng: XX XX XX GP
- Western Cape: XX XX XX WC
- KwaZulu-Natal: XX XX XX ZN
- (and so on for all 9 provinces)

**Car Model Validation:**
- Car models come from AA South Africa data
- Includes fuel tank capacity for each model
- Periodically updated when new cars come out

**Fuel Prices:**
- Current prices from PetroleumSA
- Updated when fuel prices change (regular hikes/reductions)

